      "writtenOn": "2024-01-23T22:16:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s useful for RE \u0026 HWUI for the callback to be invoked on `VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST` regardless of whether we can get detailed info from the optional `VK_EXT_device_fault` API, since we still want to crash immediately to hopefully help with stack-based clustering.\n\nThe \"generic info\" refers to the `description` strings hardcoded in the `InvokeDeviceLostCallback` implementation for different failure scenarios. Do you think those should we tweaked to clarify that Skia tried to get more info about the `VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST`, but couldn\u0027t?",
      "parentUuid": "cc907e3d_157be124",
