      "writtenOn": "2024-01-23T22:52:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah sorry yeah I should\u0027ve provided examples of what this might end up looking like when finally logged. In my current prototype of using this callback in RE, `description` ends up in a line like:\n\n\u003e RenderEngine: VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST (non-protected context): Exception type 0x1337: Cosmic tuning fork overloaded the reactor core.\n\nfor a driver-provided failure message, or:\n\n\u003e RenderEngine: VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST (non-protected context): No details: VK_EXT_device_fault not available/enabled\n\nfor a Skia-provided failure message. I\u0027m very open to changing the logging format in RE though.\n\nI feel like it\u0027s the client\u0027s responsibility to give context for the `description`, but I also definitely want the \"No details...\" `description`s that Skia provides to logically fit with what a driver might provide, so also happy to tweak those.",
      "parentUuid": "7182b04c_39f875c5",
      "range": {
